T*
(* Higher Order Derivatives: If y = f\(x\), then y_n = d^n y / dx^n. Standard nth) Tj
T*
(derivatives:) Tj
T*
(- d^n/dx^n \(e^{ax}\) = a^n * e^{ax}.) Tj
T*
(- d^n/dx^n \(\(ax + b\)^m\) = m*\(m-1\)*...*\(m-n+1\) * a^n * \(ax + b\)^{m-n}.) Tj
T*
(- d^n/dx^n \(sin\(ax + b\)\) = a^n * sin\(ax + b + n*pi/2\).) Tj
T*
(- d^n/dx^n \(cos\(ax + b\)\) = a^n * cos\(ax + b + n*pi/2\).) Tj
T*
(- d^n/dx^n \(ln\(ax + b\)\) = \(-1\)^{n-1} * \(n-1\)! * a^n / \(ax + b\)^n.) Tj
T*
(* Leibniz's Theorem on Product Differentiation: If u\(x\) and v\(x\) possess derivatives) Tj
T*
(up to nth order, the nth derivative of their product y = u * v is given by the) Tj
T*
(binomial-like expansion:) Tj
T*
(\(u * v\)_n = C\(n,0\)*u_n*v + C\(n,1\)*u_{n-1}*v_1 + C\(n,2\)*u_{n-2}*v_2 + ... +) Tj
T*
(C\(n,r\)*u_{n-r}*v_r + ... + C\(n,n\)*u*v_n,) Tj
T*
(where C\(n, r\) = n! / [ r! * \(n-r\)! ].) Tj
