(* Rolle's Theorem: If f\(x\) is continuous on [a, b], differentiable on \(a, b\), and) Tj
T*
(f\(a\) = f\(b\), then there exists at least one c in \(a, b\) such that f'\(c\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(* Lagrange's Mean Value Theorem \(LMVT\): If f\(x\) is continuous on [a, b] and) Tj
T*
(differentiable on \(a, b\), there exists c in \(a, b\) such that f'\(c\) = [ f\(b\) - f\(a\) ]) Tj
T*
(/ \(b - a\).) Tj
T*
(* Cauchy's Mean Value Theorem: For continuous f, g on [a, b] and differentiable on) Tj
T*
(\(a, b\) with g'\(x\) != 0, there exists c in \(a, b\) such that [ f\(b\) - f\(a\) ] / [ g\(b\) -) Tj
T*
(g\(a\) ] = f'\(c\) / g'\(c\).) Tj
T*
(* Taylor's Series \(Expansion about x = a\):) Tj
T*
(f\(x\) = f\(a\) + \(x - a\)*f'\(a\) + [\(x - a\)^2 / 2!]*f''\(a\) + ... + [\(x - a\)^n /) Tj
T*
(n!]*f^{\(n\)}\(a\) + R_n\(x\).) Tj
T*
(* Maclaurin's Series \(Taylor series centered at a = 0\):) Tj
T*
(f\(x\) = f\(0\) + x*f'\(0\) + \(x^2 / 2!\)*f''\(0\) + \(x^3 / 3!\)*f'''\(0\) + ... + \(x^n /) Tj
T*
(n!\)*f^{\(n\)}\(0\) + ...) Tj
