(Problem: Expand f\(x\) = e^x in powers of \(x - 2\) up to the fourth-degree term and) Tj
T*
(approximate e^{2.1}.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Evaluate derivatives at center a = 2:) Tj
T*
(f\(x\) = e^x => f\(2\) = e^2) Tj
T*
(f'\(x\) = e^x => f'\(2\) = e^2) Tj
T*
(f''\(x\) = e^x => f''\(2\) = e^2) Tj
T*
(f'''\(x\) = e^x => f'''\(2\) = e^2) Tj
T*
(f^{\(4\)}\(x\) = e^x => f^{\(4\)}\(2\) = e^2.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Substitute into Taylor's formula:) Tj
T*
(e^x = e^2 + e^2*\(x - 2\) + \(e^2 / 2!\)*\(x - 2\)^2 + \(e^2 / 6\)*\(x - 2\)^3 + \(e^2 / 24\)*\(x -) Tj
T*
(2\)^4 + ...) Tj
T*
(e^x = e^2 * [ 1 + \(x - 2\) + 0.5*\(x - 2\)^2 + 0.1667*\(x - 2\)^3 + 0.0417*\(x - 2\)^4 ].) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Evaluate at x = 2.1 \(so x - 2 = 0.1\):) Tj
T*
(Bracket = 1 + 0.1 + 0.5*\(0.01\) + 0.1667*\(0.001\) + 0.0417*\(0.0001\)) Tj
T*
(= 1 + 0.1 + 0.005 + 0.0001667 + 0.0000042 = 1.1051709.) Tj
T*
(Using e^2 = 7.389056:) Tj
T*
(e^{2.1} ~ 7.389056 * 1.1051709 = 8.16617.) Tj
T*
(Exact Value Check: e^{2.1} = 8.1661699 \(Accurate to 6 decimal places\).) Tj
T*
