T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: Evaluate the limit L = lim_{x->0} [ \(tan\(x\) / x\) ]^{1 / x^2}.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Form identification: As x -> 0, tan\(x\)/x -> 1 and 1/x^2 -> inf. This is) Tj
T*
(the 1^inf indeterminate form.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Take natural logarithm: ln\(L\) = lim_{x->0} [ ln\(tan\(x\) / x\) / x^2 ]) Tj
T*
(\(0/0 form\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Apply L'Hopital's Rule:) Tj
T*
(Numerator derivative: d/dx [ ln\(tan\(x\)\) - ln\(x\) ] = \(sec^2\(x\) / tan\(x\)\) - \(1 / x\) = \(1 /) Tj
T*
(\(sin\(x\)*cos\(x\)\)\) - \(1 / x\)) Tj
T*
(= [ 2 / sin\(2x\) ] - [ 1 / x ] = [ 2x - sin\(2x\) ] / [ x * sin\(2x\) ].) Tj
T*
(Denominator derivative: d/dx [ x^2 ] = 2x.) Tj
T*
(ln\(L\) = lim_{x->0} [ 2x - sin\(2x\) ] / [ 2x^2 * sin\(2x\) ].) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Expand sin\(2x\) using Maclaurin series sin\(u\) = u - u^3/6 + ...:) Tj
T*
(sin\(2x\) = 2x - \(2x\)^3 / 6 = 2x - \(8x^3 / 6\) = 2x - \(4/3\)*x^3.) Tj
T*
(Numerator = 2x - [ 2x - \(4/3\)*x^3 ] = \(4/3\)*x^3.) Tj
T*
(Denominator = 2x^2 * [ 2x ] = 4x^3.) Tj
T*
(ln\(L\) = lim_{x->0} [ \(4/3\)*x^3 / 4x^3 ] = \(4/3\) / 4 = 1/3.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 5: Solve for L: L = e^{ln\(L\)} = e^{1/3}.) Tj
T*
(Final Answer: Limit = e^{1/3} ~ 1.3956.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
