(Problem: Find the radius of curvature rho at the vertex \(a, 0\) of the catenary curve y =) Tj
T*
(a * cosh\(x / a\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Calculate first derivative y_1:) Tj
T*
(y_1 = dy/dx = a * sinh\(x / a\) * \(1 / a\) = sinh\(x / a\).) Tj
T*
(At x = 0 \(vertex, where y = a*cosh\(0\) = a\): y_1\(0\) = sinh\(0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate second derivative y_2:) Tj
T*
(y_2 = d^2y/dx^2 = cosh\(x / a\) * \(1 / a\) = \(1 / a\) * cosh\(x / a\).) Tj
T*
(At x = 0: y_2\(0\) = \(1 / a\) * cosh\(0\) = 1 / a.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Substitute into Cartesian curvature formula:) Tj
T*
(rho = [ 1 + \(y_1\)^2 ]^{3/2} / | y_2 |) Tj
T*
(rho = [ 1 + 0^2 ]^{3/2} / [ 1 / a ] = 1 / \(1 / a\) = a.) Tj
T*
(General Point Formula: For any point \(x, y\) on the catenary:) Tj
T*
(rho = [ 1 + sinh^2\(x / a\) ]^{3/2} / [ \(1 / a\)*cosh\(x / a\) ] = [ cosh^2\(x / a\) ]^{3/2} /) Tj
T*
([ \(1 / a\)*cosh\(x / a\) ]) Tj
T*
(= a * cosh^2\(x / a\) = y^2 / a.) Tj
T*
(Final Answer: At the vertex \(0, a\), rho = a. At any point \(x, y\), rho = y^2 / a.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
